# Markdown → JSON content pipeline

- **Single source:** `content.md` in the project root (adjust path in `scripts/sync-content-from-md.mjs` if needed).
- **Generator:** `scripts/sync-content-from-md.mjs` uses `unified` + `remark-parse` + `remark-gfm`, splits on `##` headings, maps sections to JSON files, and writes `app/data/*.json` plus `siteMeta.json`.
- **Section mapping strategy:** Use hybrid mapping (`by-heading` first, fallback `by-order`) so localized heading text can change without breaking output files.
- **Verbatim text:** Paragraphs, list items, and table cells use **source slices** (`node.position` offsets) so Markdown escapes (`\-`, `\+`, etc.) match the file. ATX headings `##`–`####` in section bodies become `ContentItem` `{ type: 'heading', level, text }` with `text` stripped of `#` markers. The app renders headings as real `<h2>`–`<h4>` and body copy via `plainContentText` (no `**`/HTML from content — style in CSS).
- **No copy edits in sync:** The sync script must never modify author intent/content from `content.md` (no auto-summarization, expansion, rewording, normalization of meaning).
- **Table cells:** Strip leading/trailing `|` from cell raw slices before saving.
- **Metadata:** `siteMeta.json` holds `title`, `description`, `url`, `locale`, `language`, `ogSiteName`, `ogImagePath`; `app/layout.tsx` imports it for `metadata` / Open Graph and `html lang`.
- **URL/locale input:** `url.txt` is the source for URL/locale values; do not hardcode per-project domain/locale in the sync script.
- **Figma tokens:** `scripts/sync-theme-from-figma.mjs` should generate `src/app/styles/theme-tokens.css`, and `globals.css` should consume these variables instead of direct hardcoded monobrand values.
- **Run:** `yarn content:sync` after editing `content.md`.
- **Porting to another project:** Copy the script + `package.json` devDependencies (`unified`, `remark-parse`, `remark-gfm`, `remark-stringify`) + `content:sync` script; rewrite the **section map** (which `##` block maps to which JSON) and component-specific shapes. If `content.md` structure changes, update the map in the script.
